1
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:25,060
Worst, best pandemic

2
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:30,960
Easily leaping over these hectic times

3
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:37,440
Diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

4
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,540
I wanna time with you one night

5
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,140
Nothing but the latest trends

6
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,080
So we can wear them

7
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,220
Because our bare faces are
sure to sell out on the spot

8
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,880
Let it rain

9
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:55,000
Everybody can do, we've started running

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,260
Dreams never stop

11
00:00:58,260 --> 00:01:02,480
Let's set sail again tomorrow

12
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,280
Let it rain

13
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:07,680
Everybody can do, just a little

14
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,860
Even if we step out of line, it doesn't hurt

15
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:15,000
Holding onto a noisy curiosity

16
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:17,400
Make it stronger, make it higher

17
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,100
Ryotsu here, still in training.

18
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:35,820
Good morning.

19
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:40,980
There's no need to be so scared, is there?

20
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:43,620
But it's a shock when it
comes out of nowhere like that.

21
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,860
What happened, Ryo-chan? Your head!

22
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:49,660
Well, actually...

23
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,360
Ryotsu got money out of the Chief...

24
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:57,540
He asked with such a serious face
that I went ahead and added it.

25
00:01:57,540 --> 00:02:00,300
Sure, there is a weekly report due, but...

26
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:02,060
We didn't call for Ryotsu, you know.

27
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:04,100
So how much did you lend him?

28
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:06,280
Well, about 70,000 yen.

29
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,540
70,000 yen?

30
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:12,700
What the hell are you doing all of a sudden?

31
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:14,180
Chief!

32
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:16,580
You money-grubbing miser!

33
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:17,620
That's harsh.

34
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:21,160
Even if you're the Chief, you've never
just yanked me from behind like that!

35
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,580
When did I ever call you by name?

36
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:25,500
Wait, that's not it.

37
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,480
Maybe I'm mistaken?

38
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:30,200
Don't you dare call me
"you," even if you die!

39
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:35,700
Today's tough love is
harsher than usual, Chief.

40
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:36,740
Of course it is.

41
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:39,820
What do you mean by deceiving
the chief to borrow money?

42
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:41,140
Deceiving the chief...

43
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:44,620
So that's how you could afford
this 70,000-yen model kit.

44
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:45,280
What?

45
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:49,919
Please don't ask me that.
I earned this by the sweat of my brow,

46
00:02:49,969 --> 00:02:51,960
bit by bit, with money I earned.

47
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:52,960
Really?

48
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:53,860
Ohoo.

49
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:58,140
Sit him down! Terai, hold his legs.
Nakagawa, his arms.

50
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:58,920
Y-yes!

51
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:04,220
W-what are you doing!

52
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:09,060
I've decided to send you to
a temple starting tomorrow.

53
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:13,360
Train at the temple for ten days and
get rid of your lustful desires for women!

54
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,720
That's basically the situation.

55
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:18,360
Well, as usual, Ryo-chan.

56
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:35,060
So that's the situation,
so please, I beg you.

57
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:38,940
Come on, Ryotsu, you ask them too.

58
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:42,020
But I'm not doing this
training because I want to!

59
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,200
And what's all this luggage?

60
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:48,880
Well, this is ten days' worth of
underwear and various other things.

61
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:52,040
I can't sleep if my pillow changes.

62
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:54,480
You're not going on an expedition to the Amazon,
you know!

63
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:55,620
Let me see.

64
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:02,920
You brought in all this worldly junk?

65
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:05,140
Do you think this counts as training?

66
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:06,620
Well, that's just it...

67
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:09,300
So that even when I look at these,
my playful urges won't stir.

68
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:11,620
I'm trying to cut off my
own temptations right now.

69
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:15,440
Everything will be kept safe at the temple.

70
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:16,880
Understood.

71
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:21,580
Earthly desires are hard to suppress,
you know.

72
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:22,420
Heh heh.

73
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:24,740
At this rate, I can get it back anytime.

74
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:26,220
Mr. Ryotsu, was it?

75
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:26,620
Yes.

76
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:29,020
In place of your secular name,
I bestow upon you

77
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,080
the treasured name Chinnen.
Have faith in it.

78
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,580
Chinnen?

79
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,860
Well then,
for a thousand and ten thousand years.

80
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:38,560
These two will be your
dedicated instructors.

81
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:40,900
Begin your training at once.

82
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:41,980
Thank you in advance.

83
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:45,140
Please.

84
00:04:54,780 --> 00:04:57,680
We've also been training for a week now.

85
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,380
I'm disappointed.

86
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:00,260
It's regrettable.

87
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:01,500
Nice to meet you.

88
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,340
Well, we eat from the same pot, after all.

89
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:05,760
Let's get along.

90
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:08,180
Hey, just leave it all to me.

91
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:11,620
Cast all worldly thoughts from your head.

92
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,580
Sit in zazen with a mind
completely free of thought.

93
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:34,420
You're still caught up in distracting thoughts,
aren't you?

94
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:36,380
How do you know that?

95
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:38,360
If you train hard like I have,

96
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:41,420
you can tell what someone like
you is thinking right away.

97
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:46,260
You just thought,
"It's obviously a lie," didn't you?

98
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:49,280
I wasn't thinking anything.
Don't make things up!

99
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,740
What's with that tone? Watch your mouth!

100
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:56,320
Don't.

101
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:58,080
Don't underestimate me.

102
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:04,260
Stinks!

103
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:15,840
Yaraa!

104
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:16,960
Yaraa!

105
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:17,860
Yaraa!

106
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:18,640
Yaraa!

107
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:19,660
Yaraa!

108
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,080
Yaraa!

109
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,737
The monks at this temple
all use swordsmanship, so

110
00:06:22,787 --> 00:06:24,640
you'd better not defy them!

111
00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:25,620
Let's run away!

112
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:49,420
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuugh...

113
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:52,760
Munen and Chinen, clean the main
hall's garden and the corridors!

114
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:54,264
Damn it,

115
00:06:54,314 --> 00:06:58,580
I knew that log pillow was weird.
So this is what it's all about!

116
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:07,680
This long

117
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,660
These temple corridors are really a pain,
you know.

118
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:13,040
You can't even see the far end, can you?

119
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,060
Wait, wait.

120
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:19,220
Doing it that way takes forever, you know.

121
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:20,400
But...

122
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:30,780
If we spread it across the full width
of the corridor like this and blow,

123
00:07:30,780 --> 00:07:32,280
we can finish in one go!

124
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:33,800
You go from that side.

125
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,620
I'll go around from this side.

126
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:38,660
But if we keep doing this,
we'll be cursed...

127
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,180
How can I eat dried squid
when I'm scared of curses?

128
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:43,620
If we run around at full speed,
it'll be done in five minutes.

129
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:45,100
That works!

130
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,540
What, you've already finished?

131
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:03,240
Yes, completely.

132
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:07,000
Don't be ridiculous.
It hasn't even been five minutes since then!

133
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,460
But it's already over, nya~.

134
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:13,280
Fine, if you're that sure,
I'll check for myself.

135
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:17,100
But if you're lying, you'd better
be prepared for the consequences.

136
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:17,800
That's right.

137
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:29,240
Rice, rice!

138
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:32,860
What is this? Is this all there is?

139
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:35,080
It's just rice porridge and pickles!

140
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:39,260
The temple serves shojin ryori,
so we don't use meat or fish.

141
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:42,100
All this vegetable stuff,
it's like being a grasshopper!

142
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,180
So you're putting up with it

143
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,840
It can't be helped.

144
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,340
This is part of the training.

145
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:49,120
Well then, let's eat.

146
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,240
I smuggled it in hidden in my underpants.

147
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,940
You guys can have some too.

148
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:00,040
No, you mustn't.

149
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,520
Eating meat is forbidden.

150
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:04,780
You'll be punished for it, you will!

151
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,740
Yeah, there's still plenty more, though.

152
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:16,640
If you guys won't eat it,
I'll just gobble it all up myself.

153
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:18,840
Itadakimasu.

154
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:24,020
Delicious.

155
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:26,700
You guys really don't want any?

156
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:29,900
Itadakimasu.

157
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:35,440
That's right,
humans have to be true to their desires.

158
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,780
You lot have real potential, you know.

159
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:45,280
What are you lot doing? Eat up!

160
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,880
I'm truly sorry, Sennen-sama.

161
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:55,420
That good-for-nothing has
done something outrageous.

162
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,620
No, I desperately tried to stop him.

163
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:59,860
He wouldn't listen to me at all.

164
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:00,860
W-what? That can't be.

165
00:10:00,860 --> 00:10:02,700
This is Sennen-san's doing.

166
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:03,420
Be quiet!

167
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:05,740
Trying to pin the blame on this holy man!

168
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:06,720
Kat!

169
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:10,720
Take responsibility: meditate in the corridor until night.
Understood?

170
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:11,660
No way...

171
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,520
My legs have gone completely stiff.

172
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:34,300
Is zazen really all there is to do here?

173
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:39,920
No radio, no TV, no manga, nothing at all.

174
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:42,940
How boring. So all we can do is sleep

175
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:44,460
You've got to be kidding.

176
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:46,640
If you don't go to sleep soon,
tomorrow will be hard.

177
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:50,040
How can I sleep when I'm this hungry?

178
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,240
Let's order sushi for delivery.

179
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:54,100
That's impossible.

180
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:58,120
Even if you could place an order,
they wouldn't deliver it to this temple.

181
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,740
Security is extremely tight.

182
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:02,440
Then we'll just go out and eat ourselves.

183
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:05,740
We can't go out.

184
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:07,740
It's fine, it's night now.

185
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:17,040
If I can just get past here, I'll be almost

186
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:18,860
What?

187
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,320
A cat?

188
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:27,260
That's one awfully big cat.

189
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:30,120
No way...

190
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:36,980
Damn it! How unlucky can I get!

191
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:46,320
They can't follow us this far, right?

192
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:51,640
Piranhas!

193
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:56,480
Crocodiles!

194
00:12:04,300 --> 00:12:05,220
Hey, Jinnu!

195
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:09,640
I won't let you escape!

196
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:13,900
Never mind that,
somebody do something about these guys!

197
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:27,540
Ryo-san isn't here?

198
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:31,420
And I came all this way to
ask for tips on this game.

199
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:35,400
Sorry, dear.
Ryo-chan is in training right now.

200
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:35,840
Tch.

201
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:39,340
Ryo-chan's actually surprisingly popular,
isn't he?

202
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:41,980
Since yesterday, people have
been asking him to fix their toys,

203
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:44,280
or asking him to teach them game tips.

204
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:46,060
Kids come by all the time.

205
00:12:46,560 --> 00:12:49,060
Senpai's always been handy
with that sort of thing.

206
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:49,820
Yeah.

207
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:54,400
I wonder what Ryo-chan's up to right now.

208
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:02,460
Well, I'm leaving the rest to you.

209
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:04,100
Take care.

210
00:13:04,580 --> 00:13:05,960
Take care.

211
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:08,080
What happened?

212
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:11,420
Apparently some high-ranking
priest has passed away.

213
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:14,300
I hear head priests from
all over Tokyo are gathering.

214
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:15,360
Yay!

215
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:17,000
So it's just us old-timers today, then.

216
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:19,500
Twist, twist!

217
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,920
Zazen, then twist!

218
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:23,700
But did we really get
the lesson done properly?

219
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:27,840
Now's our chance, now's our chance!

220
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:28,980
This, this!

221
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:37,820
That radio-controlled thing
turned out to be useful after all.

222
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:40,480
Syncing it up gave us two wins at once.

223
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:42,280
We should have done it
this way from the start.

224
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:44,400
This is bad, this is really bad,
this is terrible!

225
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:47,540
What's wrong, Ten?

226
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,600
There was a notice from ten o'clock today.

227
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:52,740
I was sure it was for tomorrow, though.

228
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:53,920
What?!

229
00:13:54,780 --> 00:13:57,700
How could we not have passed
on something this important?

230
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:00,620
What do we do? This is my fault.

231
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:01,880
Let's tell the head priest.

232
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:03,040
Wait, wait.

233
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:07,560
We can't afford to get made to kneel all
day for collective responsibility again.

234
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:10,900
I'll tell them as the
head priest's stand-in.

235
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:11,560
Shingen-san will -

236
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:12,940
Are you all right?

237
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:16,440
Nonsense,
I'm best at bluffing more than anything.

238
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,580
Leave it to me.

239
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:25,360
How's that? Doesn't look like anything but a priest,
does it?

240
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:26,620
Well, when you put it that way...

241
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:28,380
Well then, I'm off.

242
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:29,880
Have a safe trip.

243
00:14:47,580 --> 00:14:50,380
Crap, if this gets found out,
I'm a dead man.

244
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:51,240
I'm the honored one.

245
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,660
Right this way, please.

246
00:14:58,660 --> 00:14:59,680
Y-yes, yes.

247
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:16,140
Damn it, it's come to this,
I'm going all in!

248
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:22,080
Namo ami-amin erohimu essaien.

249
00:15:22,780 --> 00:15:27,380
Yarenso-ren, Kitasenju, Ayase.

250
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:29,300
Kameyari, Kanemachi.

251
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:34,140
Matsudo, Ryōgoku, Asakusa, Akihabara.

252
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:35,960
That's all.

253
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:38,780
Head priest.

254
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:40,500
Uh-oh, did they catch on?

255
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:42,691
I'm moved,

256
00:15:42,741 --> 00:15:45,680
even we can't understand
your sutra chanting.

257
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:46,320
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

258
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:49,840
Thank you for your hard work.

259
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:53,300
It's nothing. Well then, amen-double.

260
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:55,240
This is my left palm, though.

261
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:55,840
Yeah.

262
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,200
We pulled it off somehow, didn't we.

263
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:10,050
The sutra books are all kanji,

264
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:12,440
so they're completely useless to amateurs.

265
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:15,740
By the way, how much did they give us?

266
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:17,920
Wow!

267
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:21,840
I had no idea you could get this
much for one memorial service.

268
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:26,960
Welcome back! How did it go?

269
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:28,280
It was perfect.

270
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:30,280
I chanted some very blessed sutras.

271
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:31,780
That's great.

272
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:34,200
Now, let's let loose and enjoy ourselves!

273
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,600
Order ten servings of assorted sashimi,

274
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:39,300
and ten servings of meat for sukiyaki.

275
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:41,800
We'll have a party
before the monks get back.

276
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:44,260
B-but that's a lot of money...

277
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:46,902
Idiot! You're about to become a monk,

278
00:16:46,952 --> 00:16:49,220
so you can't think such worldly thoughts!

279
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:50,400
Y-yes, sir...

280
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:53,066
Worldly thoughts are no good, no good. Yes.

281
00:16:53,116 --> 00:16:57,060
Also order about two cases
of beer from the liquor store.

282
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:04,260
Cheers!

283
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:12,280
I'm spinning it a little more than usual.

284
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:13,580
Go on, go on!

285
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:14,940
Chinnen-san, check!

286
00:17:16,840 --> 00:17:17,760
A phone call

287
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:20,340
Red Snake, come on!

288
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:22,500
Here, Kiss of Fire!

289
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:25,440
Hey, Yellow, why won't you come out?

290
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,320
As if I could do that!

291
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:30,020
Chinnen-san is the best!

292
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:32,840
Come on, okay, now you, do something!

293
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:33,420
What about Warajū?

294
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:36,535
That's right,
if you can't even do one party trick,

295
00:17:36,585 --> 00:17:38,040
you'll never become a proper monk.

296
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:40,240
Trouble, trouble!

297
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:42,160
What is it, another emergency?

298
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:44,760
Chinnen-san, the head priest's

299
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:46,640
Call me Head Priest Chinnen.

300
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,780
Head Priest Chinnen.

301
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:51,340
it was a call from the head
priest's younger brother.

302
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:54,220
He caught a cold and can't attend the
memorial service he was asked to do,

303
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:56,580
so he asked if someone
could go in his place.

304
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:59,820
Very well, tell him I'll go.

305
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:00,800
Yes.

306
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:03,780
Head Priest Chinnen,
are you really sure about this?

307
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:04,940
Leave it to me.

308
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:07,380
Turning down a memorial service
would bring divine punishment.

309
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:10,480
We must not do anything that
goes against the Buddhist path.

310
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:10,980
That's right.

311
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:16,040
Everything is part of our training.
You lot, come along too.

312
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:18,700
Yahoo! I wonder how much
we'll get paid this time!

313
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:19,940
Wait, please!

314
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:36,580
Here it is! This is it, Chinnen-oshō.

315
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:49,000
Why did the Chief...

316
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,820
Master, we've been waiting for you.

317
00:18:53,020 --> 00:18:55,620
Oh crap, isn't this the
Chief's older brother's house?

318
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:58,320
Sorry to bother you when you're busy.

319
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,740
Actually, there's the pay...

320
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:02,420
Listen up, damn it.

321
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:03,780
He's my younger brother.

322
00:19:04,260 --> 00:19:04,900
Thanks.

323
00:19:05,420 --> 00:19:08,220
This is the master who kindly
came as the stand-in this time.

324
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:09,860
Thank you for having us.

325
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:11,360
The pleasure is mine.

326
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:15,800
Yamada, later.

327
00:19:29,340 --> 00:19:31,480
Looks like we can't get away like this.

328
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:33,520
What's wrong?

329
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:34,700
I was in a rush.

330
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:38,320
I mixed up the bag with the hood
and the bag with the party goods.

331
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:39,200
What?

332
00:19:40,020 --> 00:19:41,160
You mixed them up?

333
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:45,200
We can't turn back now.
We've just got to somehow keep up the act.

334
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:45,940
Yes.

335
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:09,940
They look alike.

336
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:12,140
Please be quiet.

337
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:21,060
Though we share the same sect, our customs
differ a little, so please bear with us.

338
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:24,920
The sutra may sometimes
seem faster than usual,

339
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:27,580
but each phrase carries deeper meaning.

340
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:36,220
And that concludes it.

341
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:41,220
The kanji really look that similar?

342
00:20:41,820 --> 00:20:46,120
That guy's name is Ryotsu,
a hopeless, lowest-of-the-low idiot.

343
00:20:47,840 --> 00:20:50,980
For some reason,
today it's an all-out blowout sale!

344
00:20:50,980 --> 00:20:52,920
The sutra goes on.

345
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:56,240
Excuse me, could you give me a hand?

346
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:57,220
Uh, sure.

347
00:20:57,220 --> 00:21:01,780
When chanting the sutra, go around here three times and wail,
"Waaah!"

348
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:03,520
What for?

349
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:05,420
I told you our sects are different,
didn't I?

350
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:08,160
Just do it.
You'll be struck down by divine punishment.

351
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:11,900
Why don't you do as you're told?
B-but, big brother.

352
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:12,980
Just go!

353
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:17,740
Now, I'll begin.

354
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:23,420
Gel!

355
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:28,760
Open your mouth wider and bark
"woof" while looking for your drool!

356
00:21:28,820 --> 00:21:29,960
Understood?

357
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:30,680
No way.

358
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,880
You mustn't defy me.

359
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:35,920
Doesn't that hurt, though?

360
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:38,080
If you empty your mind,
the pain doesn't hurt.

361
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:41,000
Compared to being hit with a bamboo sword,
it's nothing at all.

362
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:45,460
You have some idea what this is about,
don't you?

363
00:21:45,820 --> 00:21:48,040
Something about beating a cute
subordinate with a bamboo sword?

364
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:52,460
If you don't confess honestly,
punishment will fall on everyone here.

365
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:57,840
That's right, you remember it, don't you?

366
00:21:59,940 --> 00:22:01,200
So what about it, Daijirō?

367
00:22:01,580 --> 00:22:01,940
Yes.

368
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:07,680
Divine punishment might fall on all of you.

369
00:22:10,020 --> 00:22:11,500
Daijirō, apologize.

370
00:22:11,940 --> 00:22:15,960
If you confess in front of the eminent priest who came from Shōtenji,
you'll be forgiven.

371
00:22:17,100 --> 00:22:18,240
Shōtenji?

372
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:24,480
Excuse me, could you pick up
those reading glasses for me?

373
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:26,000
W-what are you talking about?

374
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:28,520
This is a characteristic of our sect.

375
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:30,000
Absolutely not.

376
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:30,788
Dear,

377
00:22:30,838 --> 00:22:34,400
Are you not going to listen to what I say?

378
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:42,420
I'll do it. Hey, Daijirō, Ryotsu,
there's a 10,000 yen bill lying over there!

379
00:22:42,420 --> 00:22:44,920
Where, where is it?

380
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:56,420
I knew it, this guy is definitely Ryotsu in disguise!
No, that's just a misunderstanding, it's fine.

381
00:22:56,420 --> 00:22:57,000
Nooo.

382
00:22:59,540 --> 00:23:02,420
Stop it! Can you lend anything to Mom?

383
00:23:02,540 --> 00:23:04,640
Make someone do some work!

384
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:05,400
Come on, stop it!

385
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:13,880
Chief, there's a reason for this...

386
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:18,520
Silence! I won't hear any excuses!
Go to hell!

387
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:20,140
Please stop! Chief!

388
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:27,020
Apparently they were holding a party with
sashimi and sukiyaki at the temple too.

389
00:23:27,380 --> 00:23:29,060
That's just like Ryo-chan, isn't it.

390
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:31,340
So what about the senior's training?

391
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:35,540
I've decided to have them stay at
the temple for life until they repent.

392
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:38,800
Run away! Hey, get out of here!

393
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:41,740
It's not me who can't go, it's these guys.

394
00:23:41,740 --> 00:23:43,480
If you're going to eat someone,
eat these guys instead.

395
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:47,560
If you extinguish the mind,
even fire feels cool.

396
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:49,640
Even a lion becomes a cat.

397
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:51,580
You lack training, you know.

398
00:23:51,580 --> 00:23:52,620
Chinnen-san.

399
00:23:57,360 --> 00:23:58,000
Help me!

400
00:24:05,180 --> 00:24:08,300
A seven-hour round-trip commute is insane,
you'll die!

401
00:24:08,300 --> 00:24:11,820
Leave the search for a new
dream home to me this time.

402
00:24:11,820 --> 00:24:15,340
I'll find you a house that's cheaper
and way better than the Chief's.

403
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:18,160
After all, I'm a shopping pro.

404
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:21,080
Next time: "My New Home." See you then!

405
00:24:29,020 --> 00:24:32,660
Even if you try to stop the clock,

406
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps moving on.

407
00:24:39,320 --> 00:24:42,700
Don't keep scowling,

408
00:24:44,360 --> 00:24:47,980
laugh it off and keep on living.

409
00:24:50,340 --> 00:25:03,480
Even if today is rainy,
tomorrow will be sunny.

410
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:13,860
Bye-bye,
let's wave goodbye to the bad things.

411
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:21,480
Oh yeah, let's live however we like.

412
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:23,980
Good things will come.

413
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:30,320
Outside the door, the sun is calling you.

414
00:25:43,860 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

